On ACPI the supplies take the names INT3472 registers, avdd and dovdd,
through acpi_match_device(); vd55g1 is served by an entry in int3472's
map instead. I did not add one, as it would have to say which rail each
pin feeds, and that is not known here: INT3472 calls pin type 0x10
DOVDD, while Windows' camera driver calls it Avdd. If a map entry is
preferred, I can move the names there.

